regulate|control|VERB|Control by rules or adjustment|To control how something operates or develops.|điều chỉnh; điều tiết|The valve regulates the flow of water.|Van điều chỉnh dòng nước.|Transitive.|0
pill|tablet|NOUN|Small medicine tablet|A small solid piece of medicine intended to be swallowed.|viên thuốc|The packet contains round white pills.|Gói có những viên thuốc tròn màu trắng.|Countable; no dosage instructions.|0
reliability|dependability|NOUN|Ability to be depended on|The quality of working or behaving consistently as expected.|độ tin cậy|The company tested the equipment's reliability.|Công ty kiểm tra độ tin cậy của thiết bị.|Uncountable.|0
overly|excessively|ADVERB|Too much|More than is appropriate or useful.|quá mức|The instructions are overly complicated.|Hướng dẫn phức tạp quá mức.|Before adjective or adverb.|0
oblige|require|VERB|Require someone to act|To require someone to do something because of a rule or situation.|buộc; bắt buộc|The agreement obliges them to give notice.|Thỏa thuận buộc họ phải báo trước.|Oblige someone to do.|0
oblige|help|VERB|Do a favour|To help someone by doing what they request.|giúp; làm ơn|Could you oblige me by holding the door?|Bạn có thể làm ơn giữ cửa giúp tôi không?|Oblige someone by doing; formal polite.|1
